<title>CANADA: Fidelity Canada removes fund manager - newspaper.</title>
<headline>Fidelity Canada removes fund manager - newspaper.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidelity Canada mutual fund removed the manager of its Far North Fund amid increasing scrutiny by regulators and the media, Canada's Financial Post newspaper reported.</p>
<p>Veronika Hirsh was replaced by Boston-based Alan Radlo, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Hirsh's status with Fidelity was &quot;under discussion&quot;, the report said.</p>
<p>The British Columbia Securities Commission confirmed this week it was reviewing Hirsh's personal trades in a small Vancouver junior gold company, the Financial Post said.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras (204) 947 3548</p>
</text>
